WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.11 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Identifying and assessing risk

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Describe each risk as cause, event and consequence, then score it honestly.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Look for risks in objectives, activities, money and context.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Score likelihood × impact, before and after controls.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Use scores to start a conversation, not end it.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Pan del Barrio (Social enterprise · company, Peru)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Pan del Barrio: largest office client leaves → cash shortfall; inherent 12; residual 9 with weekly invoicing.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create a risk assessment with inherent and residual scores.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
